From: Overalls maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Fail closed before snapshot publication when block drain fails

A snapshot may only be published after all submitted block work is drained and
flushed. The ordinary shutdown helper logs I/O errors and continues, which is
not a sufficient barrier for a same-memory continuation. Abort the VMM on this
error before saving transport/device state, rather than acknowledging a snapshot
that may contain an incomplete asynchronous completion queue. Lilly retains its
unfinished capture journal and cannot publish a ready checkpoint without the
successful API response.

diff --git a/src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/block/virtio/device.rs b/src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/block/virtio/device.rs
--- a/src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/block/virtio/device.rs
+++ b/src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/block/virtio/device.rs
@@ -577,4 +577,9 @@ impl VirtioBlock {
-        self.drain_and_flush(false);
+        // Snapshot publication requires a successful block barrier. A failed
+        // barrier must never be converted into a successful memory snapshot.
+        self.disk
+            .file_engine
+            .drain_and_flush(false)
+            .expect("snapshot block barrier failed");
         if let FileEngine::Async(ref _engine) = self.disk.file_engine {
             self.process_async_completion_queue();
         }
